From 5fbb0bda61263f68eb07988d974f969d7af0e6b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 14:47:02 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent: show running tasks' progress and open a task at its
 tool call
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two gaps in the task surfaces of 0037 and 0035, story 023.

The tasks card showed a running task's elapsed time, but its last tool
and tool count only on rows the user chose to watch, so a stuck task and
a busy one looked the same. Every running row now reads
"<last tool> · <N> tools · <elapsed>", or "starting · <elapsed>" before
the feed reports a tool use (a count of 0 never shows a tool), on a
second line under the description: on one line it squeezed the
description of a narrow card down to "Run...", so the description keeps
the whole first line beside its chip and controls. It follows each new
snapshot without watching or expanding the row, truncates and never
wraps, and is gone once the task ends, taking its line with it; ended
rows keep "<status> · <duration>", watched rows keep their details
(tokens, last tool, summary). Selector tasks-card-progress-{task_id}.

The Agent Tasks panel opened a past task's thread at the top, so finding
what a background script ran meant scrolling the whole conversation. The
row's open action is now "Open at Task": it opens the thread through
0040's router in its project's window, scrolled to the tool call that
started the task, where every command and edit it made is recorded.

  * history: TaskRecord gains tool_call_id, copied from the feed's
    toolCallId (0034; an empty id is treated as none). The history keeps
    it. MIGRATION: a third step is appended to HISTORY_MIGRATIONS,
    "ALTER TABLE agent_task_history ADD COLUMN tool_call_id TEXT"; steps
    0 (0035) and 1 (0039's label) are untouched, so a database written by
    an earlier Zeo opens with every record kept and a NULL id. A record
    stored without an id is filled from a later report of the same task
    (a replayed start, or its ending) through fill_tool_call_id, an
    UPDATE ... WHERE tool_call_id IS NULL: a stored id is never replaced.
    A failed fill is logged like the other history writes and memory
    keeps the id.
  * router: OpenAgentSessionOptions::tool_call_id, reserved by 0040, is
    now honoured, and gains task_id for the log line. Once the thread is
    loaded the router scrolls the ROOT thread to the ToolCall entry with
    exactly that id (not a prefix: toolu_t1 never lands on toolu_t10) and
    returns OpenedAgentSession::scrolled_to_tool_call. A subagent shown
    full screen is switched back to the root thread first, or the scroll
    would happen in a list nobody sees. An id that is not a root entry --
    a nested subagent's call, or an unknown id -- opens without
    scrolling, Ok(false), never an error. One INFO line names the
    session, task and tool call when it scrolls. The card's own
    open-at-tool-call (0037) shares the same lookup,
    agent_panel::scroll_to_root_tool_call.
  * panel: with no recorded id, or no scroll, the row says "Opened the
    thread; this task has no entry to jump to", drawn muted because it is
    an outcome, not a failure; a jump that lands clears it; a vanished
    thread keeps "Thread no longer exists" and opens nothing. Three of
    0040's assertions expected no notice after an open of a record with
    no id, and now expect that one.

Tests: agent_ui tasks_card progress 5 and progress_line 3, agent_session_router scroll 3, and
conversation_view's subagent-full-screen case 1; agent_tasks_panel
history_db tool_call_id (a database from the shipped step 0, exactly one
step appended, fills scoped to their key, never overwritten), store
tool_call_id 5, panel open_at_task 6 and tool_call_id_contract 2 (feed to
memory to disk to reload keeps the exact spelling beside case, fold and
trailing-space decoys; an id known only from disk scrolls to the exact
entry). Suites: agent_tasks_panel 121, agent_ui tasks_card 104,
agent_session_router 14.
